--- a/apps/zcode-cli/docs/provider-subscriptions.md
+++ b/apps/zcode-cli/docs/provider-subscriptions.md
@@ -459,3 +459,34 @@ builtin provider identities; previously frozen prices remain unchanged. Never fi
 speed or counters from current settings. Catalog availability and incomplete historical usage are
 different failure reasons. Published Z.AI schedules distinguish Flash/FlashX by model ID, so a missing irrelevant speed field does not block their current-rate quote; it remains unknown in usage statistics. The statistics hint identifies current/reference rate coverage without
 adding another visible report or settings page. Existing actual-payment isolation stays unchanged.
+
+### Unified cost analysis and project attribution (OV-051)
+
+One cost-analysis section replaces the unrelated model-estimate tab and subscription-payment card.
+Select either the current global usage range or one saved account/billing period. The same scoped
+request aggregates produce the API-equivalent amount, paid-fee allocation and blended per-million
+input-plus-output token rates. Fee edits update that same projection immediately; API estimates
+remain unchanged. Reuse original summary-strip and comparison-chart primitives. Published prices,
+cache discounts and recorded served speed already enter the existing ledger; do not build another
+pricing store. Show missing coverage in focused help, never invent a cost or account to fill a chart.
+Native credits remain the first allocation basis, then complete API-value weights as approved.
+Compare monetary differences only for USD payments against USD API estimates; do not invent FX.
+
+Capture workspacePath from the existing runtime workspace root in the same accounting_json fact.
+Historical missing project attribution remains a null/unassigned bucket. Compute the complete
+account-period denominator once, then project by model or workspace: the sum of project allocations,
+including unassigned work, must equal the allocated payment. Project panels later consume this same
+projection with their existing folder identity, not a separate ledger or a full monthly bill per
+project. A workspace filter applies after account-period allocation.
+
+The original context ring continues to mean conversation context pressure. Its subscription area
+must distinguish read-only quota inspection, configured default account and last actual execution
+account. Auto recovery must not relabel the default account as the account that served the request.
+Carry the existing local account ID through ModelComplete, V4 lastRequest and retained usage reads;
+never expose tokens. Keep the original popup structure and separate incomparable account windows.
+No inference-account switch or reset redemption happens from the quota-view selector.
+
+Historical usage reads do not require a configured model or active conversation. Reuse the existing
+local control-plane carrier (also used by global workflows) when no reusable local workspace client
+exists. Read the same Session SQLite ledger over v4/usage/stats; do not select an arbitrary remote
+workspace, create a conversation, start inference or add another storage owner.
